              highlighted: ["angBAK","angECG","angKAH","angGCF"] },
            { text: "so that {EC|CE} is to {CG} as {BA|AB} is to {AK},",
              visible: CON,
              highlighted: ["CE","CG","AB","AK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EC : CG = BA : AK", ref: "VI.12" }] },
            { text: "and {GC|CG} is to {CF} as {KA|AK} is to {AH}.",
              visible: CON,
              highlighted: ["CG","CF","AK","AH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "GC : CF = KA : AH", ref: "VI.12" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, ex aequali, {EC|CE} is to {CF} as {BA|AB} is to {AH}.",
              visible: CON,
              highlighted: ["CE","CF","AB","AH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EC : CF = BA : AH", ref: "V.22" }] },
            { text: "Complete the parallelogram {HB}",
              visible: HB1,
              highlighted: ["HB"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "HM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "BM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "M",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and the solid AL.",
              visible: ALL,
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "QHAK", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "ABRK", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "QKRL", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "LM",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "L",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Now since {EC|CE} is to {CG} as {BA|AB} is to {AK},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CE","CG","AB","AK"] },
            { text: "and the sides about the equal angles {ECG|angECG} and {BAK|angBAK} are thus proportional,",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angECG","angBAK"]),
              highlighted: ["angECG","angBAK","CE","CG","AB","AK"] },
            { text: "therefore the parallelogram {GE} is similar to the parallelogram {KB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["GE","KB"] },
            { text: "For the same reason the parallelogram {KH} is similar to the parallelogram {GF},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KH","GF"] },
            { text: "and also {FE} is similar to {HB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FE","HB"] },
            { text: "Therefore three parallelograms of the solid CD are similar to three parallelograms of the solid AL.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: CD3.concat(AL3) },
            { text: "But the former three are both equal and similar to the three opposite parallelograms,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: CDF },
            { text: "and the latter three are both equal and similar to the three opposite parallelograms,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ALF },
            { text: "therefore the whole solid CD is similar to the whole solid AL.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: CDF.concat(ALF),
              justifications: [{ claim: "similar solids", ref: "XI.Def.9" }] },
            { text: "Therefore on the given straight line {AB} there has been described AL",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB"].concat(ALF) },
            { text: "similar and similarly situated to the given parallelepipedal solid CD.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: CDF.concat(ALF),
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.27") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "V.22":     "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV22/",
        "VI.12":    "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI12/",
        "XI.26":    "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI26/",
        "XI.Def.9": "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI9/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Construct the solid angle contained by the angles {BAH|angBAH}, {HAK|angKAH}, and {KAB|angBAK} at the point {A} on the straight line {AB} equal to the solid angle {C} so that the angle {BAH|angBAH} equals the angle {ECF|angECF}, the angle {BAK|angBAK} equals the angle {ECG|angECG}, and the angle {KAH|angKAH} equals the angle {GCF|angGCF}, so that {EC} is to {CG} as {BA} is to {AK}, and {GC} is to {CF} as {KA} is to {AH}. [!just XI.26; VI.12]

Therefore, *ex aequali,* {EC} is to {CF} as {BA} is to {AH}. [!just V.22]

Complete the parallelogram {HB} and the solid *AL.*

Now since {EC} is to {CG} as {BA} is to {AK}, and the sides about the equal angles {ECG|angECG} and {BAK|angBAK} are thus proportional, therefore the parallelogram {GE} is similar to the parallelogram {KB}. For the same reason the parallelogram {KH} is similar to the parallelogram {GF}, and also {FE} is similar to {HB}.

Therefore three parallelograms of the solid *CD* are similar to three parallelograms of the solid *AL.* But the former three are both equal and similar to the three opposite parallelograms, and the latter three are both equal and similar to the three opposite parallelograms, therefore the whole solid *CD* is similar to the whole solid *AL.* [!just XI.Def.9]

Therefore on the given straight line {AB} there has been described *AL* similar and similarly situated to the given parallelepipedal solid *CD.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is analogous to proposition @VI.18 which constructs a similar plane figure on a line, but it is not as general since it applies only to parallelepipeds and not all polyhedra. It is not used later in the *Elements.*
